1
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:11,570
 America, America.

2
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:16,530
 There are those who say it was Christopher Columbus who discovered it five centuries ago,

3
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:20,050
 and others say it was the Vikings five centuries before that.

4
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:25,710
 It's all true, but the real first Americans, ah, that's another thing altogether.

5
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:30,110
 Alaska and Siberia were joined then, not separated as they are today.

6
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:35,140
 A period of cold back then transformed the sea into ice and snow,

7
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,400
 and the sea level dropped by 300 feet.

8
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,720
 Do you realize?

9
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:50,740
 Over on the other side, in Siberia, lived a lot of people like us.

10
00:00:50,740 --> 00:01:02,170
 You can help me to make a needle.

11
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:04,430
 Now you hold on.

12
00:01:04,430 --> 00:01:11,630
 There's nothing to eat, but pretty soon the hunters will be back, I promise you.

13
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:14,890
 Ask grandpa for a bone.

14
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:19,450
 Okay.

15
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:22,690
 Be patient, the hunters won't be long.

16
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:41,630
 The animals are getting away.

17
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:47,140
 I'm bringing much meat today.

18
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:47,730
 Shh!

19
00:01:47,730 --> 00:01:49,190
 Let me in, please take a look.

20
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:28,800
 Look, there's only one thing that means we won't have any...

21
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:33,440
 All the others gone.

22
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:44,730
 You tell us you found all that.

23
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:50,610
 Take some back.

24
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:52,130
 The others are hungry too, here.

25
00:02:52,130 --> 00:03:09,890
 To carry it if you want?

26
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:18,420
 No, I would just as soon that it'd be him.

27
00:03:18,420 --> 00:04:17,390
 Plenty of game.

28
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:32,700
 Most of times when I was younger, if you had known those days spring on me, he was enormous with teeth like sabers.

29
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:34,490
 Women ran away, we were alone.

30
00:04:34,490 --> 00:04:37,800
 Tiger and I stared back into his eyes.

31
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:42,110
 I knew he was in for a fight and then he leaped right on me, giant leap.

32
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:50,940
 I dodged him, I was upon me, I seized his tail, I whirled him around, then sent him crashing into a rock.

33
00:04:50,940 --> 00:05:15,550
 Remember too, there are no animals around.

34
00:05:15,550 --> 00:05:17,050
 Yes, they've all gone away.

35
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:18,620
 There's no good pasture land.

36
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,880
 All the grass, they're very big.

37
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:21,920
 Are we gonna starve?

38
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,610
 No, there's no reason to worry.

39
00:05:23,610 --> 00:05:26,690
 We'll follow the animals, we'll take their direction.

40
00:05:26,690 --> 00:05:48,020
 We won't put it together because tomorrow, we're on the move again.

41
00:05:48,020 --> 00:06:43,130
 Long we have walked toward the rising sun and have always found more animals and that is what we will do this time.

42
00:06:43,130 --> 00:07:57,660
 Friends migrate if they found big animals and they knew.

43
00:07:57,660 --> 00:08:04,030
 Yes, well, do they get these animals or not?

44
00:08:04,030 --> 00:08:07,030
 Patience. We shall see what we shall see.

45
00:08:07,030 --> 00:10:44,080
 And dangerous.

46
00:10:44,080 --> 00:12:27,420
 We're the two gods.

47
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:32,960
 We spear the mighty creature. We'll show you how we did it.

48
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:38,170
 Listen, all of you.

49
00:12:38,170 --> 00:12:39,770
 All killed it together.

50
00:12:39,770 --> 00:12:41,120
 Together we're strong.

51
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:43,580
 One hunter who's all alone is too weak.

52
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:46,830
 All together we're strong enough to hunt any game.

53
00:12:46,830 --> 00:12:48,540
 Tigers or the big grizzly bear.

54
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,050
 Or even the gray wolf.

55
00:12:50,050 --> 00:12:50,850
 Any of them.

56
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:53,350
 You see, hunting together,

57
00:12:53,350 --> 00:12:55,200
 we can kill the biggest animal.

58
00:12:55,200 --> 00:13:42,550
 It doesn't go away until the sun returns.

59
00:13:42,550 --> 00:15:48,930
 It's returned once again.

60
00:15:48,930 --> 00:15:51,970
 The animals have all left, we'll have to go to.

61
00:15:51,970 --> 00:15:52,960
 Go where?

62
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:56,340
 Warming sunrises, the animals have all gone that way.

63
00:15:56,340 --> 00:15:59,970
 Alright, we'll get ready.

64
00:15:59,970 --> 00:16:17,880
 That way, I will not go with you, I have come to the end of it.

65
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:23,360
 I have known many lands, crossed many rivers and mountains, I have hunted wild game.

66
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:28,240
 It is time to sleep now, to sleep of eternity, and you'll leave me.

67
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:31,900
 No! Come, Elder, we still have new lands we haven't seen.

68
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:33,980
 There are rivers we haven't crossed.

69
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:55,490
 Oh.

70
00:16:55,490 --> 00:17:07,730
 It was from one season to another, from one generation to another,

71
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:11,490
 The first Americans trudged on to the east, following the animal herds.

72
00:17:11,730 --> 00:17:14,930
 They had no idea where they were, where they were going.

73
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:20,480
 In fact, they were at a place that we call today the Bering Straits.

74
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:25,060
 But as I told you earlier back then, it was not all water as it is today.

75
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:27,890
 No, the deep cold had frozen it into ice and snow,

76
00:17:27,890 --> 00:17:31,350
 and the sea level had dropped by 100 meters, 300 feet.

77
00:17:31,610 --> 00:17:33,070
 It meant there was an earth bridge.

78
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:21,170
 It was, we just thought it was a good way to show you it was an important event.

79
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:49,270
 He's got a nice rabbit, only I couldn't quite bag him.

80
00:18:49,330 --> 00:18:52,270
 You always make up hunting stories, but the children are hungry.

81
00:19:17,610 --> 00:19:58,010
 Better go back, because now he's finding a place to camp.

82
00:19:58,390 --> 00:20:01,800
 We're going back. It's a wall of ice.

83
00:20:27,950 --> 00:20:56,030
 You, all the animals killed belong to us all.

84
00:20:57,090 --> 00:21:05,550
 Twice morsel. He was a good one.

85
00:21:06,050 --> 00:21:10,860
 And with the guts, we can make bow strings, bones for tools, and the skin will keep us warm.

86
00:21:41,410 --> 00:22:02,300
 We'd live better.

87
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:18,440
 Men wait here and see the fish as they come.

88
00:22:18,750 --> 00:22:20,590
 Right? You understand? On your way.

89
00:24:07,910 --> 00:24:08,450
 Big C.

90
00:24:12,060 --> 00:24:15,170
 He's left to hunt. We have to move on.

91
00:24:16,530 --> 00:24:18,400
 Follow the herds again.

92
00:24:57,380 --> 00:24:58,690
 and there isn't enough game.

93
00:24:59,150 --> 00:24:59,810
 We can't stay.

94
00:24:59,990 --> 00:25:01,550
 We can move on.

95
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:02,740
 Only where would we go?

96
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,060
 We might go that way,

97
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:07,280
 only there are many other people

98
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:08,100
 and not much game.

99
00:25:08,790 --> 00:25:09,230
 That way.

100
00:25:09,490 --> 00:25:10,620
 But there's no grazing land,

101
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:12,070
 so there won't be animals.

102
00:25:12,510 --> 00:25:13,160
 Or that way.

103
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:16,100
 It's my choice.

104
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:17,440
 That's the way we should go.

105
00:25:19,010 --> 00:25:19,830
 He's right, he's right.

106
00:25:19,870 --> 00:25:20,290
 Let's do it.

107
00:25:20,970 --> 00:25:22,280
 Sure he's right.

108
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:23,180
 It's the only way.

109
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:25,310
 No, no, no.

110
00:25:25,350 --> 00:25:26,210
 We don't agree at all.

111
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:27,230
 No way.

112
00:25:27,310 --> 00:25:28,850
 We're not going in that direction.

113
00:25:28,930 --> 00:25:30,610
 No, and he slapped me on the back

114
00:25:30,610 --> 00:25:31,930
 and we're not gonna go with him

115
00:25:31,930 --> 00:25:32,570
 no matter what.

116
00:25:32,650 --> 00:25:32,830
 No.

117
00:25:33,290 --> 00:25:34,280
 Do your own thing.

118
00:25:34,360 --> 00:25:35,040
 That's my motto.

119
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:36,720
 No, we're too many together.

120
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:38,740
 if we separate it into smaller ropes.

121
00:25:38,900 --> 00:25:39,380
 How's that?

122
00:25:42,660 --> 00:26:04,700
 Thousands and thousands of years

123
00:26:04,700 --> 00:26:06,780
 for that wall of ice to melt

124
00:26:06,780 --> 00:26:09,080
 the great barrier that blocked their way

125
00:26:09,080 --> 00:26:10,220
 into this new continent.

126
00:26:10,910 --> 00:26:13,990
 By now, behind them, the sea had closed in,

127
00:26:14,360 --> 00:26:15,480
 and there they were,

128
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:17,190
 the first Americans

129
00:26:17,190 --> 00:26:21,120
 on the threshold of the promised land.

